{"kind":"request","text":"E4-C: one fold for each source entry of an authorization.\n\nMeasured in `5083dc18` and `9694659a`, one run each:\n`authorizationSource` folds the journal from genesis to the source\nentry on each call. A call takes 33 to 37 ms at 1,028 rows and 137\nto 156 ms at 4,100 rows, about 35 microseconds for each row. The\nmeasured batch made six calls for two source entries.\n\nRuling: option (c) of `d2732d1e`. Keep the revisions in a map keyed\nby the hash of the source entry, and clear the map when the replica\nfolds again from genesis. The answer for a source entry never\nchanges, so the key needs no head. No rerun of the measurement: the\nchoice does not depend on the overlap with my deployment.\n\nNot now: option (b). The first fold for a source entry still costs\none pass of the journal. The state seed (SS1 to SS3) bounds that\npass, because a replica that starts at a seed holds no earlier\nentry. Say in the note where `foldThrough` starts when the replica\nhas a seed, and state the measured cost as the known limit until\nthen.\n\nConditions:\n1. One generated case in the existing owner: for any journal and\n   any source entry, the kept answer equals a fresh fold.\n2. One case counts the folds: repeated calls for one source entry\n   fold one time, and a fold again from genesis clears the map.\n3. The map holds entries of the owner's own sources only, and the\n   note states its bound.\n\nThis rides the C4 head as its own commit, or the next head that\nchanges `packages/client`. It adds no gate.","body":{"conditions":"Kept answer equals a fresh fold for generated journals. Repeated calls fold one time and a refold clears the map. The note states the map bound, the measured cost and the seed start. Rides a client head, with no gate of its own.","target_head":"3c8b8b8a1be26d3660fb2ad0a9d71b5f2315d446","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d1